## Model card

- Name: GPT-5 (OpenAI)
- Short description: OpenAI's August 2025 flagship router system pairing a fast model with a deeper reasoning model. Set launch records in math and coding, then was superseded by GPT-5.1 and later (per repo `meta.json` short).
- Provider / access: OpenAI API (Chat Completions / Responses API); ID `gpt-5`. Zen pricing per repo `meta.json`. noFreeId per repo `meta.json`.
- Release: August 2025 (per repo `meta.json` short). Knowledge cutoff: not published by vendor.
- IDs: `gpt-5` (repo meta `opencode/gpt-5`). noFreeId per repo `meta.json`.
- Context window: **400K total (128K max output)** (per repo `meta.json`); AA page shows variant "GPT-5 (deprecated)" with note that "GPT-5 (High)" exists. Scoring uses repo `meta.json` 400K figure as primary.
- Modalities: **Text, image, file in / text out; reasoning; tool calls** (per repo `meta.json`). AA confirms text+image input, reasoning yes.
- Pricing (as of 2026-10-01): **$1.25 in / $10.00 out per 1M tokens** (OpenAI, per repo `meta.json`); cached $0.125 in. Zen pricing: OpenCode Zen $1.07 in / $8.50 out per 1M. noFreeId — paid-tier only.
- Architecture: Proprietary dense transformer router (OpenAI). No parameter count disclosed.

